/**
\page Features

!!! Features
\n
!!Modular Design
Platinum is highly modular and every module builds to a separate libray. 
Library modules can depend on other modules and form a hierarchy.

\pre
                             Ptv
                              |
                             I/O
                              |
                 +------------+------------+
                 |            |            |
               System        Gfx          Text
                 |            |            |
    +------------+------+-----+           Xml
    |                   |
   Net                 Gui
\endpre

The core module is relatively small and the extentions make up
for the most part of the library. This allows the programmer to select only 
the parts of the framework that he really needs.

!! The core module
The core module provides basic types and support for object modelling. A template based 'signal/slot mechanism' and object reflection is available.

!! The I/O module
The I/O module extends standard C++ IOStreams and allows transparent and asynchronous I/O.

!! The System module
The system module provides classes for multi-threading and concurrency, file and directory management, file I/O, library loading and plugins.

!! The Net module
The networking module provides TCP and UDP I/O over various address spaces Network I/O is available through standard C++ IOStreams.

!! The Text module
The text handling module implements Unicode support and classes to encode and decode between various encodings.

!! The Xml module
The Xml module provides an Xml pull parser and an Xml writer.

!! The Gfx module
The graphics module offers support for graphics operations and drawing on images in many different color spaces (ARGB, CMYK, YUV, HSV) and for conversion between them. It extends the I/O module to allow reading and writing to various popular image formats (.jpg, .png)


!! The Gui module
The Gui module provides basic widget classes, an API for event handling and extends the drawing API of the Gfx module to allow drawing on widgets and widget back buffers.
*/

